Description: segment: -segment_list URL handlers buffer full history, never rotate
 ff_segment_muxer's `-segment_list` writes the listfile to a regular
 path by default. With `-segment_list_type csv` and a URL handler
 (http:// / https://), the listfile is HTTP-PUT-ed to the URL on
 every segment_end. The consumer (e.g. Plex Media Server) parses the
 CSV body to learn the chunk inventory.
 .
 Stock segment.c keeps a rolling window of `list_size` entries (default
 0 = streaming append, no buffering; >0 = buffer + rotate after N).
 Plex's argv bakes in `-segment_list_size 5` for HLS video AND for
 the DASH+text-subs side-channel ASS output. For URL-handler outputs,
 the rolling window is the wrong semantic: PMS expects every PUT body
 to contain the FULL chunk history, since it aggregates from the most
 recent body it received. After the 5-row window slides past, PMS
 sees a CSV missing every chunk older than 5*segment_time seconds,
 and can no longer serve them — symptoms: m3u8 playlist missing
 entries (HLS), text-sub side-channel returns 0 bytes for older
 playback positions (Plex Web SRT-burn after ~5s, observed 2026-05-14
 Plex Web Firefox FMJ 4K HDR + Dutch SRT burn).
 .
 The scaleplex worker rewriter previously bumped `-segment_list_size`
 to 99999 to work around this, but only on the main HLS path — the
 DASH+side-channel ASS output kept Plex's 5 because it lives in a
 different rewriter branch. Each new variant of "PMS sends a URL
 with list_size=5" reproduced the bug until the rewriter explicitly
 caught it.
 .
 Fix this at the source: detect URL handlers in segment_end by
 checking whether `seg->list` contains "://", and:
   * Always enter the buffering branch (regardless of list_size or
     list_type), so the listfile body contains every entry.
   * Skip the rotation drop, regardless of list_size.
 .
 File-based listfiles keep their current behaviour (list_size = N
 rotates after N entries; list_size = 0 streams single-row appends).
 The user's `-segment_list_size N` argument becomes a hint that's
 ignored for URL outputs — the only sane behaviour given the
 aggregator model.
 .
 The scaleplex worker rewriter's `-segment_list_size:5->99999` bumps
 become redundant and can be removed.
Origin: scaleplex
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-14
---
--- a/libavformat/segment.c
+++ b/libavformat/segment.c
@@ -431,7 +431,17 @@
     }

     if (seg->list) {
-        if (seg->list_size || seg->list_type == LIST_TYPE_M3U8) {
+        /* scaleplex/PLEX: when -segment_list points at a URL handler
+         * (http://, https://) the consumer is an aggregating server
+         * (e.g. Plex Media Server) that needs the full chunk history
+         * for each PUT, not the last N. Force buffering + skip the
+         * list_size rotation drop for URL outputs regardless of what
+         * the user passed for -segment_list_size. PMS's argv carries
+         * `-segment_list_size 5` baked in; without this, sub side-
+         * channel CSV rotates after 5 chunks and PMS can no longer
+         * map sub-chunk numbers to playback time. */
+        int seg_list_is_url = strstr(seg->list, "://") != NULL;
+        if (seg->list_size || seg->list_type == LIST_TYPE_M3U8 || seg_list_is_url) {
             SegmentListEntry *entry = av_mallocz(sizeof(*entry));
             if (!entry) {
                 ret = AVERROR(ENOMEM);
@@ -447,8 +457,8 @@
                 seg->segment_list_entries_end->next = entry;
             seg->segment_list_entries_end = entry;

-            /* drop first item */
-            if (seg->list_size && seg->segment_count >= seg->list_size) {
+            /* drop first item — except for URL handlers (scaleplex) */
+            if (seg->list_size && !seg_list_is_url && seg->segment_count >= seg->list_size) {
                 entry = seg->segment_list_entries;
                 seg->segment_list_entries = seg->segment_list_entries->next;
                 av_freep(&entry->filename);
